// Monster vocabulary: every monster kind, declared as an ordered entry
// list. Load assigns each id a runtime handle in entry order; handles
// are unstable across loads (entry order decides them), so saved data
// must translate through the id mapping, never store raw handles.
// A monster id declared here is only a name — kernel fields (speed, hit
// dice, …) join the entries when game logic first queries them, and how
// a monster renders lives in the display side's binding table.
[ ( monster: "giant_white_rat" ) ]
